<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Childeric I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 481</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Childeric I was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salian-franks">Salian Franks</a>, traditionally the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merovech">Merovech</a>, who ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tournai">Tournai</a> until his death around 481. He fought as an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a>. His grave, found at Tournai in 1653, held a signet ring naming him as king and gold bees, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis I</a> went on to unite the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/childeric-i.jpg" alt="Childeric I" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CHILDERICI_REGIS.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
